[% set COMPONENTS_AND_OWNERSHIP -%]
| Component | Location | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| TypeScript package | `src` | Owns production behavior and its public API |
| Test suite | `tests` | Protects public contracts and behavior |
[%- endset %]

[% set DEPENDENCY_DIRECTION -%]
Tests may depend on the public package. Production code must not depend on tests, generated output, or developer tooling.
[%- endset %]

[% set RUNTIME_DATA_FLOW -%]
No multi-component runtime flow exists in the initial scaffold.
[%- endset %]

[% set DIRECTORY_TREE -%]
```text
src/
└── index.ts
tests/
└── smoke.test.ts
```
[%- endset %]

[% set RUNTIME_CONSTRAINTS -%]
Node.js 24.18.x (>=24.18.0 <25) is required. The initial package defines no network, storage, concurrency, latency, or deployment contract.
[%- endset %]

[% set NAMING_CONVENTIONS -%]
Packages use `kebab-case`; source files, functions, methods, and variables use `camelCase` where ecosystem conventions require it; types and classes use `PascalCase`; constants use `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`; test names describe observable behavior.
[%- endset %]

[% set TECHNOLOGY_STANDARDS -%]
### TypeScript

- Use Node.js 24.18.x and pnpm 11.
- Keep TypeScript strict mode and all approved strictness flags enabled.
- Use Biome as the primary formatter, linter, and complexity enforcer.
- Use TSDoc-compatible comments for public exports and relevant `@param`, `@returns`, and `@throws` behavior.
- Keep public exports intentional and avoid untyped escape hatches.
- Add dependencies only for concrete requirements.
[%- endset %]

[% set COVERAGE_REQUIREMENTS -%]
Coverage is enforced through Vitest with the V8 provider at
[[ coverage_target ]]% across branches, functions, lines, and statements.
The `just coverage` command produces a text report.
[%- endset %]

[% set TEST_LAYOUT -%]
The base scaffold contains one public import-contract test in `tests/smoke.test.ts`. Add other test levels only for real responsibilities.
[%- endset %]

[% set TECHNOLOGY_TESTING_STANDARDS -%]
### TypeScript testing

Use Vitest for deterministic project-owned behavior and public contracts. Do not use snapshots unless serialized output is itself a stable contract.
[%- endset %]

[% set TOOLCHAIN -%]
| Concern | Standard tool | Gate |
|---|---|---|
| Runtime and dependencies | Node.js and pnpm | Pinned versions and committed lockfile |
| Formatting and linting | Biome | Zero findings with error-on-warnings |
| Static typing | TypeScript strict | Zero errors |
| Complexity | Biome | Cognitive complexity at most 10 |
| Dependency hygiene | Knip | No unused files, exports, or dependencies |
| Deduplication | pnpm dedupe | No duplicate dependencies |
| Testing and coverage | Vitest with V8 | All tests pass; [[ coverage_target ]]% branches, functions, lines, statements |
| Supply chain | pnpm audit | No unapproved vulnerabilities or invalid signatures |
| Secret scanning | Gitleaks | No verified secrets |
| GitHub Actions security | zizmor | No unapproved findings |
[%- endset %]

[% set QUALITY_GATES -%]
| Gate | Required result |
|---|---|
| Biome | No formatting, lint, or complexity findings |
| TypeScript | Zero strict type errors |
| Knip | No unused files, exports, or dependencies |
| Vitest | All meaningful tests pass with [[ coverage_target ]]% coverage |
| pnpm dedupe | No duplicate dependencies |
| pnpm audit | No unapproved vulnerabilities or invalid signatures |
| Gitleaks | No verified secrets |
| zizmor | No unapproved GitHub Actions findings |
[%- endset %]

[% set SETUP_COMMANDS -%]
pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
pre-commit install --install-hooks
[%- endset %]

[% set VERIFY_COMMANDS -%]
pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
pnpm exec biome ci . --error-on-warnings
pnpm exec tsc -p tsconfig.json
pnpm exec knip
pnpm exec vitest run --coverage
pnpm dedupe --check
pnpm audit
pnpm audit signatures
gitleaks git --redact --no-banner
zizmor --pedantic .
[%- endset %]

[% set DEVSECOPS_PROFILE -%]
Knip detects unused files, exports, and dependencies. Biome enforces
cognitive complexity. pnpm audit checks for known vulnerabilities. Gitleaks
scans repository history and zizmor analyzes GitHub Actions.
[%- endset %]
